    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 921: Minimum Add to Make Parentheses Valid (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                A parentheses string is valid if and only if every left parenthesis has a corresponding right
                parenthesis that comes later in the string. Given a parentheses string s, you can insert the
                characters '(' or ')' at any position to make it valid. Return the minimum number of
                insertions needed to make s valid.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "())"<br>
                Output: 1<br>
                Explanation: Inserting one '(' at the beginning produces "(())", which is a valid parentheses
                string.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minAddToMakeValid(string s) {
        int balance = 0, insertions = 0;

        for (char ch : s) {
            if (ch == '(') {
                balance++;
            } else {
                if (balance &gt; 0) {
                    balance--;
                } else {
                    insertions++;
                }
            }
        }

        return insertions + balance;
    }
};</code></pre>
